// src/v2/workflow/lens_discrimination_family_eval_test.dag
//
// Discrimination-lens family gate (discovered + run by the CI floor `claim_batch`
// discovery — `test data` in a `*_test.dag`, scanned across src/v2). The gate logic and
// the subject roster live in the correctly-layered discrimination-gate module
// (v2.test.discrimination_gate.*, physically under src/v2/compiler/discrimination_gate/)
// — the LENS (v2.lens.discrimination) stays a pure reader and never knows about a roster.
//
// What this gate ACTUALLY enforces (scoped honestly — DESIGN.md §6 "coverage by illusion"):
// it asserts the §5 DISCRIMINATION property — a witness unit must pair a positive
// (green-by-execution) with a PERTURBED discriminating negative (asserted red) — over a
// CURATED roster of real witness units, fail-closed (empty roster → RED) and non-vacuous
// (an all-positive control the lens must reject). This is roster/lens-correctness validation,
// NOT yet "every change in the tree is so covered": the roster is hand-enrolled, not the
// enumerated change set.
//
// Dissolve trigger toward full change-coverage: when the substrate can enumerate the change
// set structurally (the affected-set / coverage reflection blocked on .dag structural
// reflection — same wall named in lens/coverage.dag and lens/testgen.dag), feed that
// enumerated set in as the roster so the gate ranges over every change, not a curated few.
// Until then this is a bounded seed, scoped to what it proves.

module v2.test.workflow.lens_discrimination_family_eval

import v2.std.logic { Bool }
import v2.test.discrimination_gate.discrimination_roster {
  discrimination_family_gate
}

test data witness_lens_discrimination_family_gate_closed: Bool = discrimination_family_gate()
